{"id":"mahabharata-3-122","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":122,"title":"द्वाविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 122 · Chyavana and Sukanya","summary":{"en":"The aged sage Chyavana sat so long in austerity that an anthill covered him. Princess Sukanya, daughter of King Sharyati, pricked his gleaming eyes with a thorn, and when the king's army was afflicted, Sharyati gave her to Chyavana in marriage to appease him; she served him faithfully.","kn":"ವೃದ್ಧ ಚ್ಯವನ ಋಷಿ ಬಹುಕಾಲ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಕುಳಿತಿದ್ದರಿಂದ ಹುತ್ತ ಅವರನ್ನು ಮುಚ್ಚಿತ್ತು. ಶರ್ಯಾತಿರಾಜನ ಮಗಳು ಸುಕನ್ಯೆ ಹೊಳೆಯುವ ಅವರ ಕಣ್ಣುಗಳಿಗೆ ಮುಳ್ಳು ಚುಚ್ಚಿದಳು; ರಾಜನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಪೀಡಿತವಾದಾಗ ಅವರನ್ನು ಸಮಾಧಾನಿಸಲು ಶರ್ಯಾತಿ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಚ್ಯವನರಿಗೆ ಮದುವೆ ಮಾಡಿದನು; ಅವಳು ನಿಷ್ಠೆಯಿಂದ ಸೇವೆ ಮಾಡಿದಳು.","hi":"वृद्ध ऋषि च्यवन इतने लम्बे समय तक तप में बैठे कि उन पर बाँबी छा गई। राजा शर्याति की पुत्री सुकन्या ने उनकी चमकती आँखों में काँटा चुभो दिया, और राजा की सेना के पीड़ित होने पर शर्याति ने उन्हें प्रसन्न करने के लिए सुकन्या का विवाह च्यवन से कर दिया; उसने निष्ठा से उनकी सेवा की।","te":"వృద్ధుడైన చ్యవన మహర్షి చాలాకాలం తపస్సులో కూర్చోవడంతో పుట్ట ఆయనను కప్పివేసింది. శర్యాతిరాజు కుమార్తె సుకన్య మెరిసే ఆయన కళ్లను ముల్లుతో గుచ్చింది; రాజసైన్యం బాధపడగా ఆయనను ప్రసన్నం చేసుకోవడానికి శర్యాతి ఆమెను చ్యవనునికి ఇచ్చి వివాహం చేశాడు; ఆమె నిష్ఠగా సేవించింది.","ta":"முதிய ச்யவன முனிவர் நீண்ட காலம் தவத்தில் அமர்ந்ததால் புற்று அவரை மூடியது. ஶர்யாதி மன்னனின் மகள் ஸுகன்யா ஒளிரும் அவர் கண்களில் முள்ளால் குத்தினாள்; மன்னனின் படை துன்புற்றபோது அவரைச் சமாதானப்படுத்த ஶர்யாதி அவளை ச்யவனருக்கு மணமுடித்தான்; அவள் விசுவாசத்துடன் பணிவிடை செய்தாள்.","ml":"വളരെനേരം തപസ്സിലിരുന്ന വൃദ്ധമുനി ച്യവനനെ ഒരു വല്മീകം മൂടി. ശര്യാതിരാജാവിന്റെ മകൾ സുകന്യ തിളങ്ങുന്ന അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ കണ്ണുകളിൽ മുള്ളുകൊണ്ട് കുത്തുന്നു; രാജാവിന്റെ സൈന്യം പീഡിതമായപ്പോൾ മുനിയെ പ്രസാദിപ്പിക്കാൻ ശര്യാതി അവളെ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് വിവാഹം ചെയ്തു നൽകുന്നു; അവൾ വിശ്വസ്തയായി സേവിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.122; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"भृगोर्महर्षेः पुत्रोऽभूच्च्यवनो नाम भार्गवः ।\nसमीपे सरसः सोऽस्य तपस्तेपे महाद्युतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a son of the great seer Bhrigu, Chyavana of the Bhargava line. That brilliant man practised austerities beside this lake."}},{"n":2,"text":"स्थाणुभूतो महातेजा वीरस्थानेन पाण्डव ।\nअतिष्ठत्सुबहून्कालानेकदेशे विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandava, lord of the people, that greatly radiant sage stayed in one spot for a very long time, motionless as a post, in the hero's posture."}},{"n":3,"text":"स वल्मीकोऽभवदृषिर्लताभिरभिसंवृतः ।\nकालेन महता राजन्समाकीर्णः पिपीलिकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In time, O king, the seer became an anthill. Creepers covered him and ants swarmed over him."}},{"n":4,"text":"तथा स संवृतो धीमान्मृत्पिण्ड इव सर्वशः ।\nतप्यति स्म तपो राजन्वल्मीकेन समावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the wise man was wrapped on every side like a lump of clay, and went on with his austerities, hidden inside the anthill."}},{"n":5,"text":"अथ दीर्घस्य कालस्य शर्यातिर्नाम पार्थिवः ।\nआजगाम सरो रम्यं विहर्तुमिदमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long time a king named Sharyati came to this beautiful lake to enjoy himself."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्य स्त्रीणां सहस्राणि चत्वार्यासन्परिग्रहः ।\nएकैव च सुता शुभ्रा सुकन्या नाम भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He had four thousand women in his household, but only one daughter, the radiant Sukanya, Bharata."}},{"n":7,"text":"सा सखीभिः परिवृता सर्वाभरणभूषिता ।\nचङ्क्रम्यमाणा वल्मीकं भार्गवस्य समासदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by her friends and adorned with every ornament, she wandered about and came to the Bhargava's anthill."}},{"n":8,"text":"सा चैव सुदती तत्र पश्यमाना मनोरमान् ।\nवनस्पतीन्विचिन्वन्ती विजहार सखीवृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"That fair-toothed girl, looking at the lovely trees and searching among them, played there with her friends around her."}},{"n":9,"text":"रूपेण वयसा चैव मदनेन मदेन च ।\nबभञ्ज वनवृक्षाणां शाखाः परमपुष्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drunk with her beauty, her youth, love and high spirits, she broke the branches of the forest trees that were thick with blossom."}},{"n":10,"text":"तां सखीरहितामेकामेकवस्त्रामलंकृताम् ।\nददर्श भार्गवो धीमांश्चरन्तीमिव विद्युतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Apart from her friends, alone, in a single garment and wearing her jewels, she moved like lightning, and the wise Bhargava saw her."}},{"n":11,"text":"तां पश्यमानो विजने स रेमे परमद्युतिः ।\nक्षामकण्ठश्च ब्रह्मर्षिस्तपोबलसमन्वितः ।\nतामाबभाषे कल्याणीं सा चास्य न शृणोति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her in that lonely place, the radiant brahmin seer, his throat parched, was delighted, strong in the power of his austerities. He spoke to the lovely girl, but she did not hear him."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः सुकन्या वल्मीके दृष्ट्वा भार्गवचक्षुषी ।\nकौतूहलात्कण्टकेन बुद्धिमोहबलात्कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sukanya saw the Bhargava's two eyes in the anthill, and out of curiosity, her mind clouded by fate, she pierced them with a thorn."}},{"n":13,"text":"किं नु खल्विदमित्युक्त्वा निर्बिभेदास्य लोचने ।\nअक्रुध्यत्स तया विद्धे नेत्रे परममन्युमान् ।\nततः शर्यातिसैन्यस्य शकृन्मूत्रं समावृणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"What can this be?\", she pricked his eyes. The seer, with his eyes pierced, became extremely angry. Then he blocked the bowels and bladders of Sharyati's army."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततो रुद्धे शकृन्मूत्रे सैन्यमानाहदुःखितम् ।\nतथागतमभिप्रेक्ष्य पर्यपृच्छत्स पार्थिवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their evacuation blocked, the army was tormented by constipation. Seeing it so, the king asked those around him."}},{"n":15,"text":"तपोनित्यस्य वृद्धस्य रोषणस्य विशेषतः ।\nकेनापकृतमद्येह भार्गवस्य महात्मनः ।\nज्ञातं वा यदि वाज्ञातं तदृतं ब्रूत माचिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who today has wronged the great-souled Bhargava, an old man always given to austerity and quick to anger? Whether you know it or not, tell me the truth at once."}},{"n":16,"text":"तमूचुः सैनिकाः सर्वे न विद्मोऽपकृतं वयम् ।\nसर्वोपायैर्यथाकामं भवांस्तदधिगच्छतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the soldiers said to him: \"We do not know of any wrong done. Find out by every means as you please.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ततः स पृथिवीपालः साम्ना चोग्रेण च स्वयम् ।\nपर्यपृच्छत्सुहृद्वर्गं प्रत्यजानन्न चैव ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king himself questioned his circle of friends, gently and sternly, but they did not own to it."}},{"n":18,"text":"आनाहार्तं ततो दृष्ट्वा तत्सैन्यमसुखार्दितम् ।\nपितरं दुःखितं चापि सुकन्येदमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the army distressed and suffering from the blockage, and her father in sorrow, Sukanya spoke these words."}},{"n":19,"text":"मयाटन्त्येह वल्मीके दृष्टं सत्त्वमभिज्वलत् ।\nखद्योतवदभिज्ञातं तन्मया विद्धमन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While walking about here, I saw a shining creature in an anthill, glinting like a firefly, and I pierced it from close by."}},{"n":20,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वा तु शर्यातिर्वल्मीकं तूर्णमाद्रवत् ।\nतत्रापश्यत्तपोवृद्धं वयोवृद्धं च भार्गवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Sharyati ran quickly to the anthill. There he saw the Bhargava, grown old in years and in austerity."}},{"n":21,"text":"अयाचदथ सैन्यार्थं प्राञ्जलिः पृथिवीपतिः ।\nअज्ञानाद्बालया यत्ते कृतं तत्क्षन्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"With joined hands the king begged for his army: \"Please forgive what a girl did in ignorance.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीन्महीपालं च्यवनो भार्गवस्तदा ।\nरूपौदार्यसमायुक्तां लोभमोहबलात्कृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Chyavana the Bhargava said to the king: \"Your daughter, endowed with beauty and charm, did it under the force of greed and delusion.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तामेव प्रतिगृह्याहं राजन्दुहितरं तव ।\nक्षमिष्यामि महीपाल सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I take that same daughter of yours as my wife, king, I will forgive. I tell you this truly.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ऋषेर्वचनमाज्ञाय शर्यातिरविचारयन् ।\nददौ दुहितरं तस्मै च्यवनाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding the sage's words, Sharyati did not hesitate. He gave his daughter to the great-souled Chyavana."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य च तां कन्यां च्यवनः प्रससाद ह ।\nप्राप्तप्रसादो राजा स ससैन्यः पुनराव्रजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received the girl, Chyavana grew gracious. With his favour won, the king returned with his army."}},{"n":26,"text":"सुकन्यापि पतिं लब्ध्वा तपस्विनमनिन्दिता ।\nनित्यं पर्यचरत्प्रीत्या तपसा नियमेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sukanya, too, having gained an ascetic as her husband, blameless, served him always with love, with discipline and restraint."}},{"n":27,"text":"अग्नीनामतिथीनां च शुश्रूषुरनसूयिका ।\nसमाराधयत क्षिप्रं च्यवनं सा शुभानना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without envy, she tended the sacred fires and the guests, and the fair-faced woman soon won Chyavana's full favour."}}]}]}